        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Domenico Salvatori, Alessandro Moreschi, Domenico Mustafà, Giovanni Cesari\n- Concepts: castrato, castrati, classical male singing voice\n- Topics: late 19th-century singing\n\nFacts:\n- Domenico Salvatori lived from 27 September 1855 to 11 December 1909.\n- In the late 19th century, Domenico Salvatori was one of the famous castrati singers alongside Alessandro Moreschi, Domenico Mustafà, and Giovanni Cesari.\n- A castrato is a type of classical male singing voice.\n- A castrato singing voice is equivalent to a soprano, mezzo-soprano, or contralto voice.",
